266
00:18:06,454 --> 00:18:25,454
I wonder. Am I too tense today? The ball keeps bouncing off me. Gotta relax. Breathe it out. Remember that everything you've done has been for this moment.

267
00:18:25,454 --> 00:18:30,454
What are you doing, Kaneda? Hustle! Kaneda, run!

268
00:18:30,454 --> 00:18:50,454
Let us wait!

269
00:18:50,454 --> 00:18:59,454
Our plan was to counterattack by going direct all the way. But this time, they countered us instead.

270
00:18:59,454 --> 00:19:10,494
dead. It's fine. Don't worry. Just keep the momentum and we'll catch up in no time. Aim for that

271
00:19:10,494 --> 00:19:26,694
space. Asuri, look out! No! You idiot! All the way! I know that one was my fault. We gotta find

272
00:19:26,694 --> 00:19:37,534
some way to start their momentum! What is wrong with you guys? It worked. We used a high line

273
00:19:37,534 --> 00:19:42,974
to sneak in a counterattack. I knew it was a gamble and that they were afraid of what

274
00:19:42,974 --> 00:19:51,954
could happen. But they stuck it out and they took risks. This is Musashino's soccer. You

275
00:19:51,954 --> 00:19:59,854
just proved it to them. And in the most effective way. That kind of blindside is humiliating.

276
00:19:59,854 --> 00:20:05,274
Having their tactic thrown back in their faces makes the sting of giving up a goal even worse.

277
00:20:05,274 --> 00:20:10,394
This could be a blow to Aspirion's morale. They'll be at even more of a loss than ever

278
00:20:10,394 --> 00:20:15,954
after how that played out. And they've got no one to help them rally. All we have to do

279
00:20:15,954 --> 00:20:21,194
hold on! This is going to be the last action of the half! As soon as we get it, just kick

280
00:20:21,194 --> 00:20:21,614
it out!

281
00:20:24,694 --> 00:20:25,494
Over here!

282
00:20:26,134 --> 00:20:26,454
Damn.

283
00:20:32,074 --> 00:20:35,294
I have something to ask you, Muto. A favor, really.

284
00:20:36,854 --> 00:20:41,774
If you hit a long ball on the counter, or a pass in front of the goal, do you think you

285
00:20:41,774 --> 00:20:44,514
could aim it between those two for me? I'd appreciate it.

286
00:20:44,514 --> 00:20:46,014
The two over there?

287
00:20:47,014 --> 00:20:52,274
Those center backs are a weak spot. Thing is, they don't work well as a pair.

288
00:20:57,654 --> 00:21:00,514
How the hell? How'd I pull it off?

289
00:21:00,514 --> 00:21:11,994
How did I crawl my way back? By scoring. That was the only way I could console myself

290
00:21:11,994 --> 00:21:19,354
enough to go on. When I discovered skills that I lacked, I would practice every day like

291
00:21:19,354 --> 00:21:24,514
my life depended on it. I was obsessed with goals. Obsessed!

292
00:21:24,514 --> 00:21:51,834
Kuroda! Are you okay? Stretcher! We need a stretcher! Come on, man. Kuroda!

293
00:21:51,834 --> 00:22:03,774
The scoring goals. That's all he cares about. It's an obsession!

294
00:22:05,914 --> 00:22:13,214
And the first half ends with a brooist cheer, huh? Did we concede another goal? If we manage

295
00:22:13,214 --> 00:22:15,874
to keep them out, we might be able to catch up.

296
00:22:16,414 --> 00:22:20,214
Do you think so? But they were being pushed so hard.

297
00:22:20,214 --> 00:22:23,694
What? There's only one person who can rally the team.

298
00:22:24,574 --> 00:22:29,114
And I wonder how he plans to do it, considering he's only got 15 minutes for a quick pep talk.

299
00:22:33,114 --> 00:22:34,754
What do you say we go watch?

300
00:24:05,986 --> 00:24:27,766
Next time on Awashi, do your best, don't lose, fight to your limits.

